From 899d9bfc6a9d8d1403064e8647239ce836d77670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:01:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban operator: spaced '-' ends the claim window,
 "to be posted" is never a claim; deferrals take no tick slot

Follow-up to the PR #1983 review nits (t_01a1d3f6c41855df, review t_01a1d3f19d46db17).

1. Delivery claim classifier: a standalone spaced ASCII hyphen (" - ") now ends
   the governing span like ':' and the em/en dashes, so "No longer pending -
   posted to t_X." is a claim and needs the exact operator receipt. Intra-word
   hyphens ("not re-posted") are not boundaries. Controls "not posted",
   "queued", "failed and was not sent" after " - " stay non-claims.

2. Same classifier: a claim verb directly after "be" ("to be posted", "will be
   sent") is never a past claim, whatever boundary separates it from its queue
   word. "Queued to be posted", "Queued (to be posted ...)" and "Queued: to be
   posted ..." are all non-claims again; "No longer pending: posted to t_X"
   stays a claim and "has been posted" is still a claim.

3. Home executor: a call deferred for creation sync lag no longer takes a
   MAX_PER_TICK slot (the cheap replica read that decides the deferral now runs
   before the slot count and before the Board evidence read), and while the
   watermark is held below a deferral the scan pages on past SCAN_BATCH request
   rows, so later synced calls are not stalled up to CREATION_SYNC_GRACE_S.
   Without a deferral a tick still reads one batch. Deferred calls are still
   refused consent_unproven after the grace; a caller refusal still wins over
   the consent refusal.

Proof: RED on 147e0606cb: 4 classifier cases ("No longer pending - posted",
"Queued (to be posted ...)", "Queued: to be posted ...", "Done (to be
delivered ...)") and test_deferred_calls_take_no_tick_slot /
test_scan_continues_past_a_full_batch_behind_a_deferral failed. GREEN: 10
operator/consent test files, 278 passed. Mutants: 13/13 killed (be-guard,
hyphen tokenizer/boundary, deferral slot, page always/never, stop on
unreachable Board while paging, watermark hold, home refusal kept, caller
refusal precedence). Replay: old vs new claimed_targets over 81,718 real
summaries/results/comments on worker-4's boards + sync-shadow: 2 changed,
both "... to be posted ..." future forms that are now (correctly)
non-claims; no new claims from the spaced hyphen.
